cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AURORA, cite the archived version-specific software release. Insert the release DOI before publication."
title: "AURORA: Experimental Isolation for Multi-Agent Wildfire Simulation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mallampati
    given-names: Shaurya
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-07-11
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShauryaMallampati/Aurora"
url: "https://github.com/ShauryaMallampati/Aurora"
abstract: >-
  AURORA is a deterministic Python benchmark, replay, and fault-injection
  framework for experimentally isolated comparisons of multi-agent
  wildfire-response strategies. It provides event-keyed environmental
  randomness, synchronous action semantics, complete reset, causal fire-state
  labels, custom strategies, a PettingZoo adapter, replayable traces, and
  executable evidence workflows. It is not an operational or physically
  calibrated wildfire model.
keywords:
  - wildfire simulation
  - multi-agent systems
  - experimental isolation
  - fault injection
  - PettingZoo
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
